WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
Run Prompt one in the same Work chat.

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.030
Ask for an inventory that says what was
actually read, who owns

3
00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.850
it, the reporting period and any
extraction problems.

4
00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:14.200
The company brief supplies the glossary
and source-owner register.

5
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.600
The risk PDF supplies the Board targets
and context.

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.500
The workbook supplies finance inputs.

7
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.350
The customer CSV supplies counts.

8
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.900
The service JSON supplies attempts,
completions and incidents.

9
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:33.700
The growth presentation contributes a
management perspective that you will test.

10
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.616
Authority comes from the approved
definition and the person responsible for

11
00:00:37.616 --> 00:00:41.888
the source, not from whether a file is a
spreadsheet or a

12
00:00:41.888 --> 00:00:42.600
polished presentation.

13
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.700
The CFO owns revenue, variable costs and
acquisition spending.

14
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.350
Product analytics owns customer counts.

15
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.900
The CTO owns transaction counts.

16
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.206
A repeated total in a document
corroborates the underlying record; it is

17
00:00:57.206 --> 00:00:59.000
not another observation to add.

18
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.433
If a file cannot be read, name the problem
and reattach it

19
00:01:03.433 --> 00:01:05.650
rather than quietly dropping that format.

20
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:11.300
The growth presentation reports fifty-two
thousand login-active customers in June.

21
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:16.100
The customer data also records forty
thousand transacting customers.

22
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.050
This is the planned discrepancy.

23
00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:21.750
Login-active includes people who never
completed a transaction.

24
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:26.159
The executive card uses monthly
transacting customers under the company

25
00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:26.600
glossary.

26
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.150
Keep both labels.

27
00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:32.740
Do not average the totals, and do not call
the presentation mathematically

28
00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:35.800
false simply because it answers a
different question.

29
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:40.550
In the course checkpoint, forty thousand
belongs on the transacting-customer card.

30
00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:44.450
Customer origin means where the person
joined: web or mobile.

31
00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:49.408
Each person and their attributed business
activity belongs once to that origin

32
00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:52.300
even if they later use both apps.

33
00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.100
Incident surface is a separate dimension.

34
00:01:55.100 --> 00:02:00.020
An incident in the mobile app does not
establish the experience of

35
00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.250
every mobile-acquired customer.

36
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.150
Also check the two dates.

37
00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:07.500
June is the reporting month, while July
finalization allows the full thirty-day

38
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.950
activation window to mature.

39
00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.150
Pause and review your inventory.

40
00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:15.039
Continue when all six sources are
accounted for and the engagement

41
00:02:15.039 --> 00:02:16.100
distinction is clear.
